-- examples/checks/why-base.rofl — A BASE FACT WHOSE FIRING RESTS ON IT IS ITS ASSERTION.
-- wb_h(a) is asserted and also derived, from wb_c(a), which is derived from it
-- (rules/agg.rofl's `handled` and `claim` are the same shape). The shortest proof of
-- wb_c(a) is the assertion of wb_h(a), height 0, and not the circle through wb_c(a).
wb_h(a).
wb_c(X) :- wb_h(X).
wb_h(X) :- wb_c(X).
